No it doesn't. If you carry a container that contains AoY then it is the 
same as if you would carry it outside the container. The game still 
knows that you are carrying it and the power of the AoY cannot be contained.

Covetous monsters that want to steal AoY or one of the three invocation 
artifacts will steal the container containing the said item if that is 
the case. When such monster has free move (which in vanilla means that 
the monster does nothing) and has a container containing the coveted 
item, then the monster will take the coveted item out from the container 
and drops the container.

These effects continue throughout a several layers of containment. So if 
the AoY is in BoH which is in sack which is in oilskin sack then the 
wizard would try to steal the oilskin sack. Having a spare moment it 
would take the sack out of the oilskin sack and drop the oilskin sack. 
Next spare moment take the BoH out of the sack and drop the sack, then 
finally the Aoy out from the BoH and drop the BoH.

> What happens if you blow up the bag of holding containing the
> amulet?  Does it disappear, ending your chances of winning?  Fall to
> the ground?  Mysteriously appear in your inventory?

If a normal container that contains one of the four items ids distroyed 
the contens would end up in the same location where the container was.

BoH is handled differently. The item(s) end up somewhere in the dungeon. 
You need to find them again. Certain individual existing in the game can 
help you out.

> Does making the AoY unnameable affect the ability to name unidentified
